<urn:atm:triage:finding/AV3-B5>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AV3-B5" ;
  triage:title "AV.3 composition gate allowlist too narrow: rejects std prelude Option/Some/None, the AsyncMailboxRuntime trait's own method-signature types, and D2 state-handoff lifecycle states" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr ruling msg 01M1BG9Z99RSCN9A322GVQSSZW (re-verified firsthand at c9b71d720): test av3_async_mailbox_runtime_composition_rejects_read_serialization_primitives (crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs ~:3549, allowlist consumed via av3_assert_allowlisted_types ~:3991) fails against the AV.1b cutover impl in crates/atm-runtime/src/mailbox_runtime.rs, rejecting 10 symbols: (a) Option/Some/None — std prelude, unambiguous allowlist omission (Result/Ok already listed); (b) AsyncListCommand/ListOutcome/AsyncReadCommand/ReadOutcome/StateHandoffDiagnostics — the AsyncMailboxRuntime trait's OWN extended method-signature types declared in the same file (mailbox_runtime.rs:360-378); any impl must name them, so rejecting the trait's own surface is definitionally a too-narrow allowlist; (c) Unstarted/Active — D2/D2.5 state-handoff lifecycle states the contract explicitly contemplates. Ruled an AV.3 gate defect, not an AV.1b finding. Remediation suggestion: derive allowlist additions from the trait's own signatures via syn instead of hand-listing, to stop recurrence. Visible on AV.3 (c9b71d720) and AV.4 (f103e4a61) as `just lint` arch-gates 87 passed / 2 failed." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-av" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "tooling" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-31T08:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
